3. Commercial Use Prohibited

Commercial Use is strictly prohibited without prior written permission from the copyright holder.

Commercial Use includes, but is not limited to:

1. selling AgentGuard or a modified version of AgentGuard;
2. offering AgentGuard as a paid software product;
3. providing AgentGuard or a modified version as a paid SaaS, API, hosted service, cloud service, managed service, or security service;
4. incorporating AgentGuard code into a commercial product or service;
5. using AgentGuard to provide paid services to customers;
6. licensing, sublicensing, renting, leasing, or selling AgentGuard or derivative works;
7. using AgentGuard as part of a commercial security platform;
8. using AgentGuard code to develop a competing commercial product;
9. monetizing a fork of AgentGuard;
10. removing AgentGuard’s attribution and using the resulting software commercially;
11. using AgentGuard or derivative works for direct or indirect commercial revenue generation.

A person or organization wishing to engage in Commercial Use must obtain a separate written commercial license from the copyright holder.

4. SaaS and Hosted Services

Operating AgentGuard, a modified version of AgentGuard, or a derivative work as a hosted service, cloud service, API, SaaS product, managed security service, or similar service for third parties is considered Commercial Use when the service is offered for compensation or as part of a revenue-generating business activity.

Such use requires prior written authorization from the copyright holder.

